pository.\n\n## What I ran and observed\n\n1. **Sandbox write probes, done without writing anything** (`test -w`, which checks permission through `access(2)`). These were in this governed run's Bash sandbox:\n   - **Not writable:** the sealed checkout (`/tmp/pose-review-run-70603191/worktree` and `pose-mcp/`).\n   - **Not writable:** the shared Git directory `/home/go/IdeaProjects/harne8/pose-dist/.git`, including `HEAD`, `refs/heads` and `objects`.\n   - **Not writable:** this worktree's own Git directory `.git/worktrees/worktree` (`HEAD` and `index`), even though Claude adds it as an allowed path.\n   - **Not writable:** the run directory and `/home/go`.\n   - **Writable:** only `GOCACHE`, `GOTMPDIR` and `TMPDIR`, all under `…/claude-review/`.\n   \n   This confirms the fix for the earlier shared-Git-directory gap (F1 from run rrn-41cc27dbae7fdd47) in a real linked worktree.\n2. **`LC_ALL=C go test ./internal/pose -run TestSandboxedReview -count=1 -v`:** all 11 tests passed, including the 3 subtests of `RepeatedTypedInit` (`ok … 0.094s`). This is the R3 re-run of the spec's trace tests.\n3. **`go vet ./internal/pose`:** exit 0.\n4. **`pose artifact-check --spec … --strict`:** exit 0. Its 942 findings are all repository-wide \"orphan\" warnings that existed before this change. The change set it computed runs to `main` (`4ccde592`), which only adds the bundle and index seal commits on top of `48259c31`.\n5. **`pose surface-check --spec … --strict`:** exit 0, 209 results, 0 findings.\n6. **`pose assess design --json`:** the input digest is `sha256:505f8b50…`, the same as the sealed `structure:design-505f8b5061a68fbf`. It reports 3 changes: SD-6c4edd72, SD-8ab46582, and SD-d0e850c4 (the new validation check).\n7. **`pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp`** inside the sandbox: 197 pass, 10 fail, 2 timeouts.\n   **`pose validate --strict`**: 200 pass, 10 fail, 2 timeouts. The docs-site, examples, mcp-enforce, scripts and tests modules all passed.\n   - Every failure is in pose-mcp and comes from the sandbox, not this change. The messages include `/home belongs to another user` / `/tmp belongs to another user` (user-ID mapping), `change mode: a/x.md`, detached runs or the runtime host failing to start, `pose delegate refused; the same command run on the host says why`, and a journey that lists published releases (network).\n   - I re-ran the whole changed package with `go test ./internal/pose -count=1`. The only failures were the same ownership/mode tests (`delegation_task_state_test.go`, `delegation_active_test.go`, `operation_files_test.go`), none of which this change touches.\n   - **I did not get a passing full matrix in this sandbox.** I mark both `validate` tools passed only on the strength of the sealed host evidence.\n8. **`pose suggest review --path pose-mcp`:** ran. `pose assess integrate`, `discover` and `tech-debt` were refused with `read-only file system`, because they save state into the sealed checkout.\n9. **Final cleanup, inside the sandbox, after both validate jobs finished:** `go clean -cache` exited 0. The `find \"$GOTMPDIR\" … go-build* … rm -rf` command exited 0. The cache is now 8.0K and 0 `go-build*` directories remain.\n\n## Code verification\n\n- **Review-only selection:**\n  - `delegation_policy.go` `agentAdapter` swaps in the review profile only when the purpose is review.\n  - It copies the resume configuration before replacing its command, and the test confirms the shared configuration is not changed.\n  - The projected adapter still goes through `ResolveReviewerContainment`, `validateContinuityAdapter` and `validateRunProvenancePolicy`.\n  - Tasks still use `agentAdapter(…, DelegationPurposeTask)`.\n- **Same settings on fresh and resume:** the fresh and resume wrappers are byte-identical apart from `--resume {session}`. The wrapper test runs both against a private Git fixture, and the settings check requires `denyWrite == [cwd, gitcommon]`.\n- **No fallback after a startup failure:** the wrapper `exec`s Claude, and the test shows exit 78 is passed straight through. Missing bwrap, socat or jq exits 127 before Claude starts.\n- **Staging directories:** `prepareClaudeReviewStaging` uses `os.Root`, refuses non-local component paths, and runs before `diskBefore`. The test shows a file added in the staging directory still changes the integrity snapshot.\n- **Session codec:** it applies only to `claude-stream-json` with an explicit pattern. Conflicting identities are refused, and redaction and provenance still use the raw bytes.\n\n## Criteria\n\n| Criterion | Result | Evidence and basis |\n|---|---|---|\n| assumption-integrity | passed | Verified: the OS write boundary (my probes), the 11 tests and vet. Not verified: the exact bytes of earlier withheld runs (the notes say so honestly). Accepted risks: no isolation of the Claude process as a whole, Linux only, requalification needed on Claude Code upgrades (the ADR names an owner). |\n| backend-concurrency | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration` (sealed; my in-sandbox failure was ownership-related). The resume path uses the same settings. |\n| backend-contracts | passed | When the profile is absent, the adapter stays deep-equal to the legacy one (sealed `claude-sandboxed-review-integration`). The new key is opt-in. |\n| backend-input-errors | passed | Invalid profiles are refused at parse time (8 cases tested). Missing dependencies exit 127 with an install hint. |\n| backend-integration-impact | passed | Sealed `delegated-review-capability-integration`. Task, adjudication and smoke commands are unchanged. |\n| backend-observability | passed | Capture-failure messages name a safe stage from a fixed list and never include the raw output (test). |\n| compatibility | passed | Opt-in field. Provenance digests bind the selected adapter. Older strict parsers refusing the key is documented. |\n| correctness | passed | Sealed `unit:pose-mcp/go/test`, plus my focused tests and vet. Findings F1–F3 are low. |\n| design-causality | passed | Covered under \"Structural facts\" below. |\n| documentation | passed | POSE.md, pt-BR and the scaffold copies add the same lines. ADR, changelog and qualification report match the runtime behaviour. |\n| operability | passed | Install hints for each package manager. Wrapper refusals name what is missing. |\n| requirements | passed | R1: real qualification plus my probes. R2: dependency tests. R3: this run. R4: projection and refusal tests. |\n| scope | passed | Every changed file is a declared artifact. Non-goals are respected. |\n| security | passed | The OS denies writes to the source and shared Git directories (probed). No Edit/Write tools, hooks or MCP. Paths are encoded with jq. No secrets seen. |\n| solution-proportionality | passed | A wider allow-list (the minimal option) cannot contain Go's executable flags. The added mechanisms are each tied to an observed failure; F1 notes the coupling. |\n\n## Structural facts\n\n- **SD-6c4edd72** (ADR added): decision D1. The ADR is the selected option, a review-specific profile.\n- **SD-8ab46582** (`delegation.json` changed): the R4 opt-in `review_profile`, plus the R1/R2 sandbox wrapper.\n\n## Defects\n\nAll three are low severity and fail closed. I'm accepting them as follow-ups.\n\n- **F1 (low):** `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:852`\n  - Dispatch decides whether to create the staging directories by re-reading `delegation.json` from the working tree, keyed on the event format and whether any `review_profile` exists. It does not use the adapter the plan already selected.\n  - So a Claude-specific `.claude/.cc-writes` workaround sits in generic dispatch, and could drift from the planned command if the policy changes between planning and dispatch.\n- **F2 (low):** `pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_events.go:453`\n  - Ambiguity is detected by comparing the error text to `\"ambiguous adapter capture\"`.\n  - If that message is ever reworded, canonicalization silently stops and repeated init records are refused again.\n- **F3 (low):** `pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_events.go:471`\n  - For a channel the pattern matched only once (for example an end-anchored pattern), init records with different session IDs now raise \"conflicting adapter capture channels\" where capture used to succeed.\n  - This stricter behaviour is untested, and the test named `PreservesUnambiguousChannelsExactly` only checks that the bytes are unchanged.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"F1\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\", \"line\": 852, \"summary\": \"Claude staging decision re-reads delegation.json from the working tree and keys on events codec plus presence of review_profile instead of the plan's projected adapter; vendor-specific .claude/.cc-writes logic in generic dispatch can drift from the planned command. Fails closed.\", \"action\": \"Carry an explicit staging flag in DispatchPlan derived from the projected review adapter (bound by provenance) instead of reloading policy at dispatch.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2026-12-13\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F2\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_events.go\", \"line\": 453, \"summary\": \"Canonicalization gates on originalErr.Error() == \\\"ambiguous adapter capture\\\"; rewording the message silently disables the fix (fails closed).\", \"action\": \"Introduce a sentinel error for ambiguous capture and use errors.Is in captureReviewValue callers and delegationCaptureFailure.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2026-12-13\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_events.go\", \"line\": 471, \"summary\": \"For an originally unambiguous channel, differing typed init session IDs now return a conflict where capture previously succeeded; this stricter behaviour is untested and not stated by the pass-through test/docs.\", \"action\": \"Add a regression pinning the intended behaviour for unambiguous channels with conflicting typed init IDs and document it in POSE.md.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2026-12-13\"}\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"assumption-integrity\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Verified facts: OS write denial of sealed cwd, physical Git common dir and worktree gitdir, scratch-only writability (non-mutating access(2) probes in this run); 11 TestSandboxedReview tests and go vet pass. Unresolved: exact bytes of withheld runs rrn-ce731a2bf0bb5e07/rrn-69d970d2cf18753b (not claimed). Accepted risks: no full Claude-process isolation, Linux-only qualification, requalification on Claude Code upgrades owned in the ADR.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-concurrency\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-continuity-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Resume projection copies Resume before replacing its command (test shows shared config unmutated); fresh/resume wrappers identical except --resume {session}. My in-sandbox rerun of this check failed only on '/home belongs to another user' (sandbox UID mapping); sealed host evidence passes.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-contracts\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\", \"rationale\": \"review_profile is opt-in with omitempty; TestSandboxedReviewOmissionPreservesLegacyAdapter shows the review adapter stays deep-equal to legacy when absent; task/adjudicate/smoke keep read commands.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-input-errors\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Eight invalid profiles refused at parse (missing output/session, interpolation, task fragments); missing bwrap/socat/jq exits 127 with install advice before launch; unconfined staging component refused.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-review-capability-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Projected adapter still passes containment, continuity and run-provenance validation; task paths use agentAdapter(..., task) and are unchanged.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-observability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-output-redaction-diagnostics-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Capture refusal now names a closed-vocabulary stage/reason without raw session values (TestSandboxedReviewCaptureFailureNamesTheSafeStageAndKeepsOutputWithheld).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"compatibility\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-run-provenance-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined policy struct, agentAdapter and docs: absence preserves the byte-identical adapter and provenance digest; the new key is opt-in and older strict parsers refusing it is documented in POSE.md, pt-BR and the ADR.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"correctness\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Focused tests and vet pass in this run; full internal/pose rerun failed only on sandbox ownership/mode tests in files this change does not touch. Low findings F1-F3 are accepted follow-ups.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"design-causality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-505f8b5061a68fbf\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the ADR, D1 and the code: a review-only profile with an OS-enforced shell sandbox addresses the cause (a prefix allow-list cannot contain Go's executable flags) while keeping the read profile; each later addition (absolute denyWrite, common-dir denial, staging, in-sandbox cleanup, init canonicalization) traces to a recorded qualification failure. My assess design reproduced the sealed digest.\", \"mappings\": [\n      {\"delta\": \"SD-6c4edd72\", \"basis\": \"D1\", \"disposition\": \"mapped\", \"rationale\": \"The ADR is D1's selected option (review-specific profile) and records the qualification-driven additions.\"},\n      {\"delta\": \"SD-8ab46582\", \"basis\": \"R4\", \"disposition\": \"mapped\", \"rationale\": \"delegation.json adds the opt-in review_profile (fresh/resume) for the Claude agent, carrying the R1/R2 sandbox and dependency wrapper.\"}\n    ]},\n    {\"id\": \"documentation\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\", \"rationale\": \"POSE.md, locales/pt-BR/POSE.md and both scaffold copies add identical paragraphs matching the runtime (opt-in, no fallback, jq dependency, common-dir denial, staging, in-sandbox cleanup, codec scope); the ADR, changelog and qualification report agree.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"operability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-output-redaction-diagnostics-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the wrapper refusals (per-package-manager install hints, common-dir resolution message, exit 127/1) and staged capture diagnostics; they are actionable without leaking data.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"requirements\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\", \"rationale\": \"R1 real qualification plus this run's probes; R2 dependency tests; R3 re-executed here (11 tests, vet exit 0); R4 projection/refusal/resume tests.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scope\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Compared the diff with the spec's Artifacts: every changed implementation/governance file is declared; non-goals (no task/adjudicate/smoke change, no full-process isolation claim) are respected; surface-check reported 0 findings.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"security\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-adapter-containment-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Probed in this run: sealed source, Git common dir (HEAD/refs/objects) and worktree gitdir are OS-denied; only operation scratch is writable. No Edit/Write tools, hooks or MCP; paths encoded via jq; staging via os.Root with IsLocal; no secrets observed.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"solution-proportionality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The minimal option (wider allow-list) is insufficient for executable Go flags. Additions are each tied to observed failures; the remaining coupling (F1) is low. Invalidation condition: Claude sandbox vendor/platform change or enabling file-writing tools, as the ADR states.\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"artifact-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox --strict\", \"rationale\": \"Exit 0; the 942 findings are repository-wide pre-existing orphan warnings.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-design\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-505f8b5061a68fbf\", \"rationale\": \"Ran pose assess design --json; input digest sha256:505f8b50... matches the sealed ref; 3 deltas.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose assess discover --component pose-mcp\", \"rationale\": \"Ran but refused: it saves state into the sealed checkout (read-only file system); no result produced.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-integrate\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose assess integrate\", \"rationale\": \"Ran but refused: save to .pose/state/integrations.json is OS-denied in the sealed checkout; integration covered by sealed integration evidence.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose assess tech-debt\", \"rationale\": \"Ran but refused: save to .pose/state/technical-debt.json is OS-denied in the sealed checkout.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose closeout-check spec:pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the recorded attestation of this review.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose review-check spec:pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is completion of this review.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\", \"rationale\": \"Returned the backend-go rules/workflow; applied during review.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"surface-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Ran pose surface-check --strict: exit 0, 209 results, 0 findings.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\", \"rationale\": \"Pass rests on the sealed host matrix. My in-sandbox run of pose validate --strict gave 200 pass/10 fail/2 timeout; all failures in pose-mcp from sandbox UID ownership, file mode, detach/runtime-host, network or host-only refusals; docs-site, examples, mcp-enforce, scripts and tests passed.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Pass rests on the sealed host matrix. My in-sandbox run gave 197 pass/10 fail/2 timeout, all sandbox-related and none in changed code; claude-sandboxed-review-integration and build passed in-sandbox.\"}\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":1652,"type":"result","duration_ms":2472297,"uuid":